\caption(Even/odd transforms and one negative-imaginary twiddle reproduce all four complex coefficients.)
\alttext(Bars show input samples one through four. A second panel separates real and imaginary DFT coefficients, with a positive imaginary value at bin one. Tables report every coefficient and independent transform, inverse and energy checks.)

>> Do not double DC or Nyquist

With eight samples at eight samples per second, construct
x_t=2+3*cos(2*pi*t/8)+.5*(−1)^t. The DC magnitude is 16, the conjugate pair at
bins one and seven has magnitude 12 each, and Nyquist has magnitude four.
The one-sided amplitudes are therefore two, three and .5. Mean square is
2^2+3^2/2+.5^2=8.75; Nyquist's alternating samples have mean square .25, not .125.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fft_amplitude.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  using namespace dm::algorithms;
  std::vector<double> x(8), time;
  for (int t = 0; t < 8; ++t) {
    time.push_back(t / 8.);
    x[t] = 2 + 3 * std::cos(2 * std::numbers::pi_v<double> * t / 8) + .5 * (t % 2 ? -1 : 1);
  }
  const auto s           = fft_spectrum(x, 8);
  double     mean_square = 0;
  for (double v : s.numeric_column("mean_square").values())
    mean_square += v;
  if (std::abs(s.double_at("amplitude", 0) - 2) > 1e-12 ||
      std::abs(s.double_at("amplitude", 1) - 3) > 1e-12 ||
      std::abs(s.double_at("amplitude", 4) - .5) > 1e-12 || std::abs(mean_square - 8.75) > 1e-12)
    throw std::runtime_error("one-sided calibration mismatch");
  auto signal = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), amplitude = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  signal.line(time, x, "samples", {37, 99, 235})
      .points(time, x, "observed", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .title("Offset, cosine and alternating component")
      .x_label("time (s)")
      .y_label("sample value")
      .y_limits(-2, 8);
  amplitude
      .bars(
          s.numeric_column("frequency").values(),
          s.numeric_column("amplitude").values(),
          "amplitude",
          {220, 38, 38},
          .5)
      .title("DC and Nyquist keep their own weight")
      .x_label("frequency (Hz)")
      .y_label("one-sided amplitude")
      .y_limits(0, 4.5);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(signal)
      .add(amplitude)
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/fft_amplitude.svg");
  std::print("{}\n\nSum of per-bin mean-square contributions: {:.9f}.\n", s.to_md(9), mean_square);
}
```
