| index | full_linear | period_four |
| ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 1 | 5 |
| 1 | 3 | 3 |
| 2 | 5 | 5 |
| 3 | 7 | 7 |
| 4 | 4 | nan |


Period-four bin zero: 5.000000000; full linear first plus final: 5.000000000.
\image(figures/fft_convolution.svg)
// result_end
\caption(A sufficiently padded spectral product computes linear convolution; a shorter period computes a different circular operation.)
\alttext(Five linear output bars are compared with four circular output bars. The latter start at five because the final linear coefficient four wraps into the first coefficient one. The fifth circular table entry is undefined, not zero.)

> Checking the theory

>> Direct sums, inverse residuals and energy test different properties

For power-of-two lengths 2..256, construct a bounded deterministic complex
sequence with varying real and imaginary parts. Each row compares FFT coefficients
to an extended-accumulation direct DFT, checks the complex inverse and tests Parseval.
The plotted error values are logarithms, with a display floor of 1e-18 for exact-zero
residuals. The first plot counts DFT summands and FFT butterflies, whose costs differ;
it illustrates growth orders and is not a stopwatch benchmark. Relative errors are
reported in scientific notation so small residuals do not appear as rounded zeros.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fft_checks.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  using namespace dm::algorithms;
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame   table;
  std::vector<double>      lengths, logn, direct_count, fast_count, forward_error, inverse_error;
  std::vector<std::string> ftext, itext, etext;
  for (std::size_t n : {2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256}) {
    std::vector<std::complex<double>> x(n);
    for (std::size_t t = 0; t < n; ++t)
      x[t] = {
          std::sin(.37 * t) + .2 * std::cos(.11 * t),
          .5 * std::cos(.23 * t) - .1 * std::sin(.61 * t)};
    const auto d = fft_diagnostics(x);
    const auto f = d.double_at("relative_dft_error", 0),
               i = d.double_at("relative_inverse_error", 0),
               e = d.double_at("relative_energy_error", 0);
    if (f > 2e-12 || i > 2e-12 || e > 2e-12)
      throw std::runtime_error("transform identity check failed");
    lengths.push_back(n);
    logn.push_back(std::log2(n));
    direct_count.push_back(std::log10(double(n) * n));
    fast_count.push_back(std::log10(n * std::log2(n) / 2));
    forward_error.push_back(std::log10(std::max(1e-18, f)));
    inverse_error.push_back(std::log10(std::max(1e-18, i)));
    ftext.push_back(std::format("{:.3e}", f));
    itext.push_back(std::format("{:.3e}", i));
    etext.push_back(std::format("{:.3e}", e));
  }
  table.add_column("length", lengths);
  table.add_column("relative_dft_error", ftext);
  table.add_column("relative_inverse_error", itext);
  table.add_column("relative_energy_error", etext);
  auto counts = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), errors = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  counts.line(logn, direct_count, "DFT summands", {220, 38, 38})
      .line(logn, fast_count, "FFT butterflies", {37, 99, 235})
      .title("Operation structures have different growth")
      .x_label("log2 transform length")
      .y_label("log10 count, not elapsed time")
      .y_limits(0, 6);
  errors.line(logn, forward_error, "DFT comparison", {37, 99, 235})
      .line(logn, inverse_error, "complex inverse", {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Independent coefficient and inverse checks")
      .x_label("log2 transform length")
      .y_label("log10 relative maximum error")
      .y_limits(-18.5, -11);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(counts).add(errors).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/fft_checks.svg");
  std::print("{}\n", table.to_md(0));
}
```
