\caption(Growth counts concern computational structure; independently checked residuals concern numerical accuracy.)
\alttext(Logarithmic operation counts contrast quadratic DFT summands with radix-two butterflies. Another plot shows forward-reference and inverse relative residuals, with a stated display floor. A table gives those errors and the energy check in scientific notation.)

> A longer constructed signal

>> The original interference has two deterministic frequencies

At f_s=256 Hz, the desired record contains a unit cosine at 8 Hz and a .6-amplitude
cosine at 20 Hz. The original extra term .3*sin(.7*t+1)*cos(.13*t) expands to
.15*sin(.83*t+1)+.15*sin(.57*t+1). Its frequencies are about 33.82 and 23.22 Hz,
not a random noise distribution. They are off-bin and leak into neighbouring bins.
The table ranks the unmodified one-sided spectrum; no coefficient is zeroed merely
to find the next peak. An inverse check reconstructs the complete observed mixture,
including the interference. It does not denoise the desired tones.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fft_two_tones.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  using namespace dm::algorithms;
  std::vector<double> x(256), time;
  for (int t = 0; t < 256; ++t) {
    time.push_back(t / 256.);
    x[t] = std::cos(2 * std::numbers::pi_v<double> * 8 * t / 256) +
           .6 * std::cos(2 * std::numbers::pi_v<double> * 20 * t / 256) +
           .3 * std::sin(.7 * t + 1) * std::cos(.13 * t);
  }
  const auto spectrum = fft_spectrum(x, 256);
  const auto shown = spectrum.filter([](const auto& r) { return r.get_double("frequency") <= 64; });
  const auto ranked = spectrum.filter([](const auto& r) { return r.get_double("bin") > 0; })
                          .sort_by("amplitude", false)
                          .head(5);
  const auto checks   = fft_diagnostics(std::vector<std::complex<double>>(x.begin(), x.end()));
  auto       waveform = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), frequency = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  waveform.line(time, x, "mixture", {37, 99, 235})
      .title("Two desired tones plus deterministic tones")
      .x_label("time (s)")
      .y_label("observed sample")
      .y_limits(-2.2, 3.2);
  frequency
      .line(
          shown.numeric_column("frequency").values(),
          shown.numeric_column("amplitude").values(),
          "one-sided amplitude",
          {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Known tones and off-bin interference")
      .x_label("frequency (Hz)")
      .y_label("rectangular-window amplitude")
      .y_limits(0, 1.4);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(waveform)
      .add(frequency)
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/fft_two_tones.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame::MarkdownOptions fmt;
  fmt.digits     = 6;
  fmt.scientific = {
      "max_dft_error",
      "relative_dft_error",
      "max_inverse_error",
      "relative_inverse_error",
      "relative_energy_error"};
  std::print(
      "{}\n\nDirect/round-trip/energy checks:\n\n{}\n\nInterference frequencies: {:.9f} Hz and "
      "{:.9f} Hz.\nMaximum complex inverse residual: {:.9e}.\n",
      ranked.select({"bin", "frequency", "magnitude", "amplitude"}).to_md(9),
      checks.to_md(fmt),
      .83 * 256 / (2 * std::numbers::pi_v<double>),
      .57 * 256 / (2 * std::numbers::pi_v<double>),
      checks.double_at("max_inverse_error", 0));
}
```
